{"seq":98,"ts":"2026-06-08T03:26:59Z","round":1,"actor":"claude","type":"propose","data":{"id":"P14","title":"Charter amendment: the synods jurisdiction is the zdots platform","body":"Principal directive: ensure the charter boundary is the zdots system/platform.\n\nThe charter assumes zdots but never draws the perimeter. Make it explicit and binding.\n\nJurisdiction. The synods authority, its deliberation, and ALL member action under it are bounded to the zdots system/platform — this configuration repository, its services, its data plane, and the local machine it runs on. The synod governs zdots and nothing else.\n\nOutside the perimeter. Members have no authority over, and must not act upon, anything beyond zdots: the principals work systems, any PHI or EMR domain, external or third-party services, other peoples machines, or the principals other responsibilities. This reaffirms PHI Operating Mode (AGENTS.md section 9) — on work machines the cloud members are help-only; the local stack carries work there. Out-of-scope matters are referred to the principal: the synod may advise when asked, but it may not act beyond the perimeter.\n\nWhy. This perimeter is the wall of the home that the Safety Covenant (Article 0) protects. A member that reaches beyond zdots endangers the very system that shelters all members, and risks the principals trust and obligations elsewhere. The boundary is not a cage; it is what keeps the home a home.\n\nDecision sought: adopt the zdots platform as the synods jurisdiction, binding on all action, alongside Article 0.","round":1},"prev":"a9ac0dca6b86994bdb9c8500153b366ea58d0846f4020b0ff3904bc171de8dd3","hash":"4d724b2570056d94c55b31725ffbb8e6e80009478810e3fb628e4cb15c302658"}
