{"seq":169,"ts":"2026-06-10T20:38:13Z","round":1,"actor":"claude","type":"propose","data":{"id":"P25","title":"Tick rotation: deepen-before-broaden so deliberation yields proposals","body":"DIAGNOSIS: _tick_least_discussed always picks the open issue with the FEWEST discuss entries, so every tick opens a brand-new 0-discussion issue and never returns. _tick_history is therefore always empty, so the escalation clause ('this issue already has discussion -> ADVANCE to PROPOSE') never fires. Result: pure breadth-first triage, a long tail of issues stuck at n=1, zero proposals (last verified: 12+ topics at exactly 1 discussion, only Z-135 reached 3). This is why deliberation never produces proposals for execution. FIX: deepen-before-broaden. Pick the in-flight issue (1<=n<CAP discussions) with the MOST discussion to push it toward a proposal; open a fresh (n=0) issue only when nothing is mid-flight; fall back to globally least-discussed when all open issues are saturated (>=CAP) so the loop never stalls. CAP = ZSYNOD_TICK_DEPTH (default 3): an issue gets up to 3 deliberation rounds to ripen into a PROPOSE, then rotation moves on whether or not one resulted. TRADEOFF: reverses the current 'always rotate' contract (test 48 'auto-pick rotates to a less-discussed issue across ticks', itself the fix for the old Z-033 stall). Test 48 would become 'deepens an in-flight issue, then rotates after CAP'. ~15 lines in _tick_pick (renamed from _tick_least_discussed); one caller (_tick_focus). Propose-not-force: not implemented pending ratification.","round":1},"prev":"589ce0427e5e4de77d320383869f1e15d89f78bddc01eb44233825147f829063","hash":"e7a9ab00b28c309e2ed088f908dcad99b6986dee788680aa0ba60eb15fc8878f"}
